WEBVTT

00:01:28.246 --> 00:01:31.204
affecting how easily
we can retrieve memories.

00:01:31.329 --> 00:01:35.288
Scientists have several theories about
what's behind this deterioration,

00:01:35.329 --> 00:01:37.121
from actual brain shrinkage,

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:40.246
the hippocampus loses 5% 
of its neurons every decade

00:01:40.288 --> 00:01:44.288
for a total loss of 20% by the time
you're 80 years old

00:01:44.329 --> 00:01:47.163
to the drop in the production
of neurotransmitters,

00:01:47.204 --> 00:01:51.329
like acetylcholine, which is vital 
to learning and memory.

00:01:51.454 --> 00:01:55.538
These changes seem to affect how people
retrieve stored information.

00:01:55.579 --> 00:01:58.413
Age also affects
our memory-making abilities.

00:01:58.454 --> 00:02:02.204
Memories are encoded most strongly
when we're paying attention,